IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, Part 7 (Money Laundering) and Schedule 9 -- LAYER 1, NOUNS ONLY.
-- Target: main (checked on build 1.6.109).  Nouns only: DECLAREs, no rules, no directives.
-- Only a noun that two or more modules use is declared here; a record that belongs to one section sits in that section's module.
-- Field names start at the complement (no `is` / `has` before the complement), because the genitive supplies the verb.

-- The three parts of the United Kingdom the Act names (s 327(1)(e): England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland;
-- s 335(7) and s 336D(9): the part of the UK in which the person is, or in which the application is made).
DECLARE `Part of the United Kingdom` IS ONE OF
    `England and Wales`
    Scotland
    `Northern Ireland`

-- To whom a disclosure under Part 7 can be made (ss 330(4), 331(4), 333A(2), 335(1), 337(4), 338(1)(a), 339ZA).
-- s 340(13): a reference to a constable includes a person authorised for the purposes of Part 7 by the Director General of the
-- National Crime Agency; this noun keeps that person separate so the inclusion can be seen.
DECLARE `Person to whom a disclosure is made` IS ONE OF
    `a constable`
    `a customs officer`
    `an officer of Revenue and Customs`
    `a nominated officer`
    `a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency`
    `anyone else`

-- The offences of Part 7 that have a penalty clause of their own or that s 334 prices (ss 334, 333A(4), 336(6), 339(1A), 339ZH(8)).
DECLARE `Offence under Part 7` IS ONE OF
    `an offence under section 327, 328 or 329`
    `an offence under section 330, 331 or 332`
    `an offence under section 333A`
    `an offence under section 336(5)`
    `an offence under section 339(1A)`
    `another offence`

-- How a fine is capped when the text caps it by reference to something outside Part 7 (the "statutory maximum", "level 5 on the standard scale")
-- or does not cap it ("or to a fine").  The number behind the first two is not in the sources.
DECLARE `Ceiling of a fine` IS ONE OF
    `the statutory maximum`
    `level 5 on the standard scale`
    `a fine with no ceiling stated`

-- A person who is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser (ss 330(14), 333E(5)).
DECLARE `Adviser` HAS
    `professional legal adviser`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `accountant, auditor or tax adviser`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `member of a professional body established for accountants, auditors or tax advisers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body makes provision for testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership as a condition for such admission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body makes provision for imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body makes provision for imposing sanctions for non-compliance with those standards` IS A BOOLEAN

-- How a person is convicted of a Part 7 offence (ss 334, 333A(4), 336(6)).
DECLARE `Way of being convicted` IS ONE OF
    `on summary conviction`
    `on conviction on indictment`

-- What a penalty clause lets a court impose: a ceiling, never a tariff (the clause says "not exceeding", "or to a fine", "or to both").
-- Months are whole months; an Act that says "five years" is 60 months, "14 years" 168 months.
DECLARE `Penalty ceiling` HAS
    `months of imprisonment`                   IS A NUMBER
    `ceiling of the fine`                      IS A `Ceiling of a fine`
    `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The people the Part's duties and prohibitions are put on (for the regulative rules and their #TRACEs).
DECLARE `Party under Part 7` IS ONE OF
    `the person`
    `the nominated officer`
    `the constable or officer of Revenue and Customs`

-- The things those people do or must not do.
DECLARE `Act under Part 7` IS ONE OF
    `give the appropriate consent to a prohibited act`
    `make the required disclosure`
    `disclose a matter within section 333A(2)`
    `disclose the contemplated or actual investigation`
    `disclose in full to a person authorised by the Director General of the National Crime Agency`
    `make a disclosure otherwise than in the prescribed form or manner`
    `tell a person of an information order`
    `comply with a requirement of an information order`
    `include in a relevant disclosure information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency`
    `notify an NCA authorised officer that a joint disclosure report is not being made`
    `conceal, disguise, convert, transfer or remove criminal property`
    `enter into or become concerned in an arrangement which facilitates the acquisition, retention, use or control of criminal property`
    `acquire, use or have possession of criminal property`
